<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">12 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 12 July, from 927 to 1997.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/aethelstan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelstan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/927">927 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,099 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Æthelstan receives the submission of northern rulers at Eamont</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Eamont, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penrith">Penrith</a>, four rulers, among them King Constantine II of Alba, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hywel-dda">Hywel Dda</a> of Deheubarth and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ealdred-of-bamburgh">Ealdred of Bamburgh</a>, accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelstan">Æthelstan</a>'s overlordship. Seven years of peace in the north followed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelstan">Æthelstan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hywel-dda">Hywel Dda</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1191">1191 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">835 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Acre surrenders to the armies of the Third Crusade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege of almost two years, the garrison of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I</a> and Philip II. The port became the crusaders' main base and later capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1335">1335 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">691 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Benedict XII issues a bull to reform the Cistercians</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Sorgues, Pope Benedict XII issued the bull Fulgens sicut stella matutina to reform the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cistercians">Cistercian Order</a>. It prescribed economic consolidation of indebted houses, compulsory attendance at the general chapter, stricter discipline and reorganised theological studies for monks.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cistercians">Cistercians</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1470">1470 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">556 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Ottomans capture Negroponte and the island of Euboea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> personally led the Ottoman siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euboea">Negroponte</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcis">Chalcis</a>), capital of the Venetian possession of Euboea. After almost a month, and despite heavy losses, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took both the city and the island.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1543">1543 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">483 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VIII marries Catherine Parr, his sixth wife</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> married the twice-widowed Catherine Parr at Hampton Court. She outlived him, helped reconcile the king with his daughters and became the first English queen to publish a book in her own name.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1691">1691 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">335 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Williamite army wins the Battle of Aughrim</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">William III's forces under Godert de Ginkel defeated the Jacobite army at Aughrim in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-galway">County Galway</a> (12 July Old Style). The bloodiest battle in Irish history effectively decided the Williamite war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1862">1862 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">164 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln signs the act creating the Army Medal of Honor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Lincoln signed a resolution authorising the Medal of Honor for army soldiers who distinguished themselves by gallantry. It remains the highest US military decoration.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet and German tanks clash at Prokhorovka</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet tank armies counter-attacked the SS Panzer Corps at Prokhorovka, one of the largest tank battles in history. The Soviets lost heavily, but the German offensive at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kursk">Kursk</a> was halted.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1997">1997 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">29 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Malala Yousafzai is born in Pakistan's Swat Valley</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Malala Yousafzai was born in Mingora. Shot by the Taliban in 2012 for campaigning for girls' education, she survived and in 2014 became the youngest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> laureate.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 12 July <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-yoshinori"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ashikaga-yoshinori.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ashikaga Yoshinori</span><span class="tp">1394–1441</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-chanel"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pierre-chanel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pierre Chanel</span><span class="tp">1803–1841</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hipolito-yrigoyen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hipolito-yrigoyen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hipólito Yrigoyen</span><span class="tp">1852–1933</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emil-hacha"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emil-hacha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emil Hácha</span><span class="tp">1872–1945</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pablo-neruda"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pablo-neruda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pablo Neruda</span><span class="tp">1904–1973</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tupou-vi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tupou-vi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tupou VI</span><span class="tp">b. 1959</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 12 July <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bertrada-of-laon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bertrada-of-laon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bertrada of Laon</span><span class="tp">c. 720–783</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/meng-chang"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Meng Chang</span><span class="tp">919–965</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-yoshinori"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ashikaga-yoshinori.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ashikaga Yoshinori</span><span class="tp">1394–1441</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/erasmus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/erasmus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Erasmus</span><span class="tp">1466–1536</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alexander-hamilton"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alexander-hamilton.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alexander Hamilton</span><span class="tp">c. 1755–1804</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfred-dreyfus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfred-dreyfus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfred Dreyfus</span><span class="tp">1859–1935</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/douglas-hyde"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/douglas-hyde.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Douglas Hyde</span><span class="tp">1860–1949</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
